e2e-evidence/BASE.md text eol=lf

# ── E2E-P2.8 / R-BP (c): pin LF for every path a test reader slices ─────────
# P6.1e's gate went red on a clean tip for an environment reason:
# Git-for-Windows' SYSTEM config sets core.autocrlf=true on this box, so a fresh
# checkout writes CRLF while the blob is LF, and every suite that slices product
# source on a newline-anchored marker silently degraded to an empty fragment
# (tests/e2e-web-frame-classifier.test.mjs reported 0/1 instead of 174/174 — a
# green that was never capable of being red). The readers now normalise at the
# read site; this pins the other half, so the working tree matches the blob no
# matter what autocrlf says. `git add --renormalize` over these paths is a no-op.
# The attributes file itself, so the rule that pins everyone else does not
# drift to CRLF on this box.
.gitattributes text eol=lf
hooks/** text eol=lf
lib/** text eol=lf
tests/** text eol=lf
scripts/** text eol=lf
# The brief says `extension/**`; the directory in this repo is `chrome-extension/`.
chrome-extension/** text eol=lf

# Binary guards. `chrome-extension/** text` would otherwise mark the toolbar
# icons as text, and a PNG's 8-byte signature IS `\x89PNG\r\n\x1a\n` — CRLF
# inside a header. Normalising it rewrites those two bytes and the icon stops
# decoding. The rule above is a glob over a directory, so the exclusion has to
# be explicit rather than inferred.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff2 binary

# ── OUT OF LANE, REPORTED TO KEN (P2.8 STOP, item 3.2) ─────────────────────
# These six blobs are committed with MIXED CRLF/CR/LF line terminators. Under
# `scripts/** text eol=lf` every one of them would be rewritten by
# `git add --renormalize`, and the brief is explicit that a mass line-ending
# commit is not this lane's to make. Left `-text` (as-is, exactly today's
# behaviour) so the rule above cannot rewrite them and cannot leave the tree
# permanently dirty either. None is read or sliced by any suite, so nothing in
# the gate depends on them. They want their own one-line renormalisation lane.
scripts/ext-badge-sidepanel-proof.mjs -text
scripts/ext-dock-gesture-proof.mjs -text
scripts/ext-in-call-shots.mjs -text
scripts/ext-indicator-proof.mjs -text
scripts/ext-sidepanel-shots.mjs -text
scripts/ext-templates-scroll-call-message-proof.mjs -text
